  "extraction_notes": [
    "Curves digitized from a 400 dpi raster; Fig.1 traced continuously per temperature (the two curves stay separated, no crossing within the plotted range). Estimated read error about +/-0.005 V (Fig.1), +/-10 percent of value (Fig.2), +/-0.03 pF (Fig.3).",
    "Digitized values are consistent with the table: Fig.1 25 degC gives VF = 0.333 V at 1 mA (max 0.38 V) and 0.653 V at 30 mA (max 1.0 V); Fig.2 25 degC gives IR = 0.069 uA at 30 V (max 0.2 uA).",
    "Capacitance row is labelled 'Type junction capacitance' (sic) but its 5.0 pF value sits in the Max column; recorded as maximum. The Fig.3 typical curve reads about 3.6 pF at VR = 0 V.",
    "In forward_voltage_points the current entries are the exact specified test conditions (source_kind 'typical'); the voltage entries are datasheet maxima.",
    "No breakdown row exists; VRRM = VDC = 40 V (p. 1) are absolute maximum ratings, not measured breakdown, so breakdown fields are null.",
    "Fig.4 Power Derating Curve (p. 2) was not digitized: thermal derating, not an electrical characteristic of the junction.",
    "Additional ratings on p. 1: VRRM = 40 V, VRMS = 28 V, VDC = 40 V, IF(AV) = 200 mA, IFSM = 600 mA @ 8.3 ms half-sine, PD = 200 mW, Tj max +125 degC, RthJA = 500 degC/W.",
    "Manufacturer footer full name: Zhuhai Hongjiacheng Technology co., Ltd (www.ichjc.com)."
  ],
